# Large STAT cache — 2.4 GB, auto-fetched by stat/fetch.py (all of
# stat_fetch/data/ is fetch-stage cache/checkpoints; stat_filter/data/ holds
# the actual final outputs — runs.tsv etc. — and stays tracked)
stat/fetch/data/*
!stat/fetch/data/manifest.tsv

# Intermediate confirmed-run caches — regeneratable from stat_cache
stat/filter/data/*_confirmed.json

# Large species distribution table (38k rows)
stat/filter/data/*_species_dist.tsv

# Reference DB source files — auto-downloaded by stat/build.py
stat/build/data/phi-base_current.csv
stat/build/data/ictv_vmr.xlsx

# meta_search.py raw API response caches — regeneratable
metadata/search/data/bp_cache.json
metadata/search/data/bs_cache.json
metadata/search/data/serper_cache.json

# meta_text.py: manually-downloaded copyrighted journal PDFs (715MB+, and not
# ours to redistribute) — never committed. Its .bak sibling is working-copy
# cruft, also excluded.
metadata/text/data/manual_pdfs/
metadata/text/data/text_cache.jsonl.bak

# The repo is for code (+ small figures/manifests to discuss results), not
# data — 2026-08-31 policy, purged from history at the same time. These are
# all locally regeneratable (or synced to Setonix directly, outside git) —
# see the module docstrings/READMEs for how each is produced.
metadata/search/data/bioprojects.json
metadata/search/data/biosamples.json
metadata/text/data/text_cache.jsonl
metadata/classify/data/samples.tsv
metadata/classify/data/classify_cache.jsonl
metadata/classify/data/host_disambig_cache.jsonl
stat/build/data/phibase_db.json
stat/filter/data/runs.tsv
stat/filter/figures/scatter_data.tsv

# legacy/ dirs (superseded scripts + their outputs, kept on disk for local
# reference only) — excluded from the repo entirely rather than picking
# through individual files; simpler, and none of it is needed anywhere
# downstream (nothing reads from legacy/, matching kraken/legacy/ having been
# fully wiped rather than kept at all — see kraken/README.md "History").

# Log history dirs + .latest symlinks are now TRACKED (transparency — Leon's
# call 2026-09-01: full run history should be visible in the repo, not just
# code). Do not re-add exclusions for logs/history/ or logs/*.latest here.

# Stray BUSCO container job logs that end up at repo root on Setonix
/busco_*.log
busco_downloads/

# Kraken2 classify cache — large, regeneratable on Setonix
kraken/assign/data/kraken_cache*.jsonl
kraken/assign/data/kraken_cache*.txt
kraken/assign/data/reports/
kraken/assign/data/reports_v1/

# Old output/ directory — local pipeline data, all superseded by module layout
/output/

# Claude Code project settings
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Colleague correspondence / external documents
kristina/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.env

# Kraken2 large files (reproducible, not tracked)
kraken/utilities/pilot/kallisto/indices/
kraken/utilities/pilot/kallisto/quant/
kraken/utilities/pilot/kallisto/reads/
kraken/utilities/pilot/kallisto/refs/
kraken/utilities/pilot/kraken/kraken_db/
kraken/utilities/pilot/kraken/reads/

# Kraken2 pipeline data — lives on Setonix scratch (~200GB: CDS downloads, BUSCO
# lineage caches, Kraken2 DBs, downloaded FASTQ). Ignore the data by exact subdir
# name (small tracked TSVs — ref_candidates.tsv, busco_scores.tsv, manifest.tsv —
# live alongside these in the same data/ dirs and stay tracked). manifest.tsv
# (generated by manifest.py, at repo root) records what exists remotely without
# holding the data itself. See memory/kraken_restructure_plan.md.
# Paths updated 2026-09-25 for the flattened module/<step>/ layout (kraken/db/search
# -> kraken/search, kraken/db/utilities -> kraken/utilities, etc.). The four kraken/db/
# entries below were missed when the structure moved and left the Setonix data dirs
# unignored; db_v3 added at the same time. kraken_run_download/ dropped entirely.
kraken/search/data/cds/
kraken/utilities/busco/data/busco_downloads/
kraken/utilities/busco/data/busco_scan_cache.tsv
kraken/build/data/db_v2/
kraken/build/data/db_v3/
kraken/build/data/db/
kraken/select/data/reads/
kraken/utilities/split/data/index/
kraken/utilities/split/data/reads/
kraken/utilities/split/data/_tmp/

# FracMinHash sketch cache — one .npy per assembly (~700 MB on Setonix), the only
# expensive part of kraken_db_saturation.py and fully rebuilt by --stage sketch.
# The curve/bias/policy stages read it and write the small TSVs, which stay tracked.
kraken/utilities/saturation/data/sketches/

# Stray SLURM .out/.err that older kraken scripts dropped at the repo root on
# Setonix before every --output path pointed at kraken/slurm/logs/.
/*.out
/*.err

# Ensembl Plants REST species list — cache for kraken_hosts.py geo lookups, refetched
# if absent, not needed on Setonix (which downloads via --from-table). The ignore here
# pointed at the pre-flatten path and so never applied; the file is now tracked at
# kraken/search/data/ensembl_species.json (84 KB). Left tracked deliberately — untrack
# with `git rm --cached` if the cache should stay local-only.

# Personal reference/prose: pipeline schematic, literature notes, manuscript drafts.
# Kept on disk for navigation, not version-controlled (Leon's call 2026-09-24).
docs/
